body:
Looking in the code, I found a similar case for Spring which seems fixed by `BlacklistedServletContainerInitializerBuildItem`. 

I Added this code to the Sentry recorder which fix the bug. 
```
 @BuildStep
    public BlacklistedServletContainerInitializerBuildItem blacklistServlet() {
        return new BlacklistedServletContainerInitializerBuildItem("io.sentry.servlet.SentryServletContainerInitializer");
    }
```

I think this is a good thing at the end because we had no control over this `SentryServletContainerInitializer ` which was always enabled. Now I need a way to add our own sentry servlet initializer managed by us to replace it :)
